cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "LoRa CFO Headroom Map: Re-verifying a LoRa Demodulator Baseline and Mapping Where Classical CFO Estimation Stops"
authors:
  - name: "haegwon"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gwon9906/lora-cfo-headroom-map"
url: "https://github.com/gwon9906/lora-cfo-headroom-map"
abstract: >
  An independent re-verification study of LoRa (Chirp Spread Spectrum) ultra-low-SNR
  demodulation. Starts from an attempt to use a Complex-valued Bidirectional
  Associative Memory (BAM) as a denoising front-end, finds that the apparent gain was
  recovered front-end implementation loss rather than learned denoising, and
  self-falsifies that result and its first replacement twice over. Separately
  reproduces a published neural-enhanced LoRa demodulator (NELoRa, SenSys'21) on its
  public benchmark release and finds its reported baseline is missing a band-limiting
  step present in the original LoRaPHY implementation it is ported from; restoring that
  step closes most of the reported gap. The surviving, defensible contribution is a
  genie-bounded headroom map: where classical CFO (carrier frequency offset) estimation
  stops paying, quantified with bootstrap confidence intervals, across a baseline ladder
  from blind to drift-aware 2D estimation.
keywords:
  - LoRa
  - chirp spread spectrum
  - low-SNR demodulation
  - carrier frequency offset
  - signal processing
  - reproducibility
license: "MIT"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-03"
